WWP REMOTE ACCESS - FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS
IT Helpdesk  |  x4100  |  helpdesk@{{ ww_domain }}          Updated 2026-07-09
==============================================================================

Q: How do I connect from home?
A: Use the WWP VPN client (FortiClient) installed on your WWP laptop. Server:
   vpn.{{ ww_domain }}. Sign in with your normal username (e.g. j.doe) and
   password, then approve the push in the Authenticator app.

Q: What can I reach on the VPN?
A: Email, Teams, the file server (S: Public, plus your department share),
   timekeeping, Cityworks and the intranet. The VPN puts you on the CORPORATE
   network only.

Q: Can I look at plant trends from home?
A: Yes - the process historian has a read-only web trend viewer that is
   reachable from the corporate network/VPN:
       http://ww-hist01:8080   ({{ ww_net }}.30.10)
   Ask Operations for a login; the guest view shows the main plant tags.

Q: Can I get to the SCADA / HMI over the VPN?
A: No. The SCADA control network is separated from the corporate network.
   Control room staff use the HMI on site. IT and approved vendors reach the
   control network only through the OT jump server, following the OT Remote
   Access SOP (Engineering share). If you think you need OT access, talk to
   Marcus Oyelaran (x4310).

Q: I'm a vendor/contractor. How do I get access?
A: Document and plan downloads are on the contractor portal,
   https://portal.{{ ww_domain }}. Vendors needing SCADA support access are
   handled by Engineering under their service contract - not by the helpdesk.

Q: My VPN connects but the S: drive is missing.
A: Open File Explorer and browse to \\ww-fs01\Public. If you get a password
   prompt, use your WWP username/password. Still failing? Call x4100.

Q: I forgot my password / I'm locked out.
A: Call the helpdesk during business hours (7:00-4:30 M-F). After hours, call
   the control room (x4220) and they will page on-call IT. We will verify your
   identity using your employee ID and supervisor before resetting.

Q: Can I use my personal computer?
A: Not for VPN. Webmail (with MFA) is fine from a personal device.
